            <title>[LU-21150] runtests test_1: client mount after server restart times out, MGS requests never sent (sent delay, rc = -110)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21150</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;runtests test_1 on a DNE review session (el9.7, review-dne-part-2, ldiskfs) restarts all servers and remounts the clients. The client mount then fails twice with "mount.lustre: mount ... failed: Connection timed out" (rc = -110) and runtests carries on against an unmounted /mnt/lustre, so the later checks report "Post remount. Files differ: rc=2" (or "statmany ... failed", "No such file or directory").&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client debug log: every MGS connect request (o250 to MGC10.240.23.246@tcp) expires after 1s with "Request sent has timed out for sent delay: &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;sent N/real 0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;" and err -110, i.e. the request was never put on the wire. The MGS node's dmesg shows nothing for the attempt. The client console then logs "MGC10.240.23.246@tcp: Confguration from log lustre-client failed from MGS -110. Communication error between node &amp;amp; MGS".&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The cluster stays unusable for the rest of the session: sanity-lfsck fails its setup with the same client mount timeout ("NAME=autotest_config not mounted"), and sanity-sec and pjdfstest then fail setup with "mountoss failed" because the OST5 to OST8 dm-flakey devices were never created after the aborted sanity-lfsck setup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test set: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/fd2cc0c6-1f05-4636-b550-81bbf2d94431" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/fd2cc0c6-1f05-4636-b550-81bbf2d94431&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Session: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/0920c0e1-ee00-45c0-9d0a-120fa9e0d051" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/0920c0e1-ee00-45c0-9d0a-120fa9e0d051&lt;/a&gt; (change 70512 patchset 1, which only touches osc_cache_writeback_range() and cannot affect the client mount path).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-70512-ps1-e30395889540 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/70512" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/70512&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
